module multi_aspect_objective

// PRD v0_6 multi-aspect-objective-units-coherence §δ headline: a coherent
// multi-aspect objective — Money AND Mass combined in ONE dimensionless
// `minimize` term — solves end-to-end. Task δ (#5020) integration-gate
// example (BT4 positive; the negative sibling is
// `multi_aspect_objective_mixed.ri`, BT1).
//
// A part has its own material thickness (stress/clearance requirement:
// thickness ≥ 2mm, same idiom as `examples/continuous_cost_min.ri`). Both
// material cost AND mass grow with thickness, so the design wants to
// minimise a WEIGHTED COMBINATION of the two aspects — but cost is Money and
// mass is Mass, and summing incommensurable dimensions directly is
// physically meaningless (that is exactly what α's compile-time guard,
// `DiagnosticCode::ObjectiveDimensionIncoherent` / `E_OBJECTIVE_MIXED_DIMENSION`,
// rejects — see the sibling negative fixture). The coherent idiom this file
// ships is to NORMALISE each aspect to a dimensionless ratio before summing:
//
//   minimize unit_cost*(thickness/1mm)/1USD + w*mass_per_mm*(thickness/1mm)/1kg
//
// Both summands are dimensionless (Money*dimensionless/Money and
// Real*Mass*dimensionless/Mass), so the inner `+` is dimension-honest and,
// being ONE term, never reaches the multi-term coherence guard (that guard
// only fires for `terms.len() > 1`). `w` is a dimensionless weight trading
// off the two normalised aspects.
//
// Integration test:
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/multi_aspect_objective_example_e2e.rs
//   asserts no `ObjectiveDimensionIncoherent` (compile AND eval) and
//   `thickness` resolves to a finite, feasible Length strictly above the
//   2mm constraint boundary.
//
// # Why the solver parks at the seed instead of the 2mm boundary
//
// The objective is dimensionless (not Money), so `objective_is_money` is
// false and NO robustness floor is synthesised (contrast
// `continuous_cost_min.ri`, whose Money objective DOES get a floor). Both
// summands increase with `thickness`, so Nelder-Mead drives toward the 2mm
// lower bound, drifts sub-boundary, becomes infeasible, and falls back to
// the initially-feasible SEED (~10mm) via the `initially_feasible` fallback
// (`crates/reify-constraints/src/solver.rs`) — landing well off the boundary
// without any floor mechanism. This is the same seed-fallback behaviour
// `continuous_cost_min.ri` documents, just without the floor diagnostic.
//
// # Why auto(free), not strict auto
//
// A strict `auto` triggers the uniqueness re-solve (perturbing the start and
// checking convergence within `UNIQUENESS_SD_TOLERANCE`). Because the
// eval-layer solver returns the initially-feasible SEED rather than a unique
// convergent point, the perturbed re-solve does not reconverge to the same
// value, and `ConstraintNonUnique` would mask the result. `auto(free)` skips
// the uniqueness check here — feasibility and dimension-coherence are the
// concerns, not uniqueness. Same reasoning as `continuous_cost_min.ri`.
//
// # Why a plain structure (not Costed/Massive conformance)
//
// `unit_cost` and `mass_per_mm` are plain closed-form params scaled by
// `thickness`, not the frozen `Costed`/`Massive` trait fields (those aspects
// and their `.sum` cross-scope aggregation idiom are proven by
// `examples/aspect_massive.ri`, task β). Cross-scope aggregation over
// children is out of scope here — task #4785's territory — this example's
// job is the single-scope objective-COMBINATION seam: normalising and
// summing two aspects into one coherent term.
structure MultiAspectPart {
    param thickness : Length = auto(free)
    param unit_cost : Money = 5USD
    param mass_per_mm : Mass = 0.2kg
    param w : Real = 0.5

    // Stress/clearance minimum-thickness, same idiom as continuous_cost_min.ri.
    constraint thickness > 2mm

    // ONE normalised dimensionless objective term combining both aspects:
    // Money*(dimensionless)/Money = dimensionless; Real*Mass*(dimensionless)/Mass
    // = dimensionless. Dimension-honest `+`, single ObjectiveTerm — never
    // reaches the multi-term coherence guard.
    minimize unit_cost * (thickness / 1mm) / 1USD + w * mass_per_mm * (thickness / 1mm) / 1kg
}
